# Test: an admin command form posts its argument value through the daemon
# VALIDATES: AC-1 of spec-both-help-texts-reach-every-surface. The page for
# `clear firewall domain-group` renders one input for the `name` leaf its
# `-cmd` module declares under the ze:command container with both texts
# (internal/component/firewall/plugins/domain/yang/ze-firewall-domain-group-cmd.yang),
# so the form shows the summary and the explanation. A value typed into it is
# carried into the command the web server dispatches: the result card's title
# is the dispatched command, `clear firewall domain-group name blocked`,
# keyword before value, and its body is the dispatcher's answer.
#
# The command is a `-cmd` leaf on purpose. The admin form reads the node's
# ArgDefs, which extractArgDefs (internal/component/config/yang/command.go)
# fills from the leaves of the ze:command container alone. An rpc input leaf
# of the `-api` module reaches the API and MCP schemas (AC-2, AC-6), never the
# command tree, so a builtin whose only declaration was such a leaf rendered
# NO input here. `system command help` was one until 2026-09-15; its page is
# admin-command-help-posts-name.wb.
# PREVENTS: HandleAdminExecute building the command from the URL path alone,
# so the typed value is dropped in silence and the daemon answers for the
# bare command. The web suite starts `ze start --web-only`, whose dispatcher
# (webOnlyDispatcher, cmd/ze/hub/service_web.go) answers every operational
# command with the standalone-mode message, so the answer the card carries is
# that message: it proves the POST reached the dispatcher and its answer came
# back to the card, and the title proves what the dispatcher was handed.

option=timeout:value=30s

action=open:path=/admin/clear/firewall/domain-group
expect=element:text=clear firewall domain-group
expect=element:text=Domain group name
expect=element:text=A group from the firewall configuration.
action=fill:id=param-name:value=blocked
action=click:text=Execute
expect=element:text=clear firewall domain-group name blocked
expect=element:text=running in standalone mode
expect=element:not-text=panic
